# Cathode — standalone repository ignore rules.
#
# The plugin lives at `Cathode/`. Rules are path-anchored (leading `/`) so they bind to these
# locations and nowhere else.

# --- Vendored third-party library SOURCE (reserved; populated by the plugin's install.sh) ---
# The 5 upstream libs (quickjs-ng, litehtml, harfbuzz, blend2d, asmjit) are cloned at pinned
# commits, never committed — install.sh reproduces them from its pin table on any checkout.
/vendor/

# --- Cathode vendor-lib BUILD OUTPUTS ---
# `include/` and `Win64/` under each ThirdParty lib are build artifacts, not source: they are
# produced by the vendor build from the gitignored `vendor/` sources. Each lib dir keeps a
# tracked `.gitkeep` so the directory shape survives without its contents.
/Cathode/Source/ThirdParty/*/Win64/
/Cathode/Source/ThirdParty/*/include/

# --- Authoring/ Node toolchain (dev-machine/CI only) ---
# `node_modules/` and the IIFE build output `dist/` are not committed; package.json +
# package-lock.json are, for a reproducible `npm ci`. The plugin subtree carries its own
# `Cathode/Authoring/.gitignore` with these same two rules; these root entries are belt-and-braces.
/Cathode/Authoring/node_modules/
/Cathode/Authoring/dist/
